<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yaghma</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Yagma</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yaghma were a Turkic tribe of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, living in the 10th century around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashgar">Kashgar</a> and the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarim-basin">Tarim Basin</a> and associated with the Toquz Oghuz. Together with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chigils">Chigils</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karluks">Karluks</a> they formed the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kara-khanid-khanate">Kara-Khanid Khanate</a>, and some historians trace the dynasty itself to them. Mahmud al-Kashgari recorded their speech in the 11th century.</p></div>
